{#
  The one confirmation on the project-details page.

  Everything that asks before it acts renders through this fragment: a service's own
  ``DeploymentAction`` (sleep, wake) and the project's dangerous actions (deleting a
  project, deployment, component or attachment; reprocessing). It is loaded into the
  shared modal shell by openServiceModal(), so there is one dialog with one set of
  rules instead of a second one that has to remember them.

  Expects: action (DeploymentAction or ProjectAction), key, message. Optional: blocked_reason.

  The endpoint is filled in server-side from the action itself; this template never
  sees a URL from the request.

  The CSRF header lives on the wrapping div, NOT on the button: htmx inherits it from an
  ancestor, and a ROOS <c-button> re-emits attribute values in double quotes, which
  mangles the JSON of hx-headers.

  On confirm the endpoint answers with the shared progress fragment and htmx swaps it
  into this dialog, replacing the question with the running task. That is the whole
  reason these actions are tasks: they commit to git and then run the reprocessing
  pipeline, ArgoCD sync included, so there is real progress to follow rather than a
  request to wait out -- and while it runs, the progress view is what keeps the dialog
  from being dismissed.
#}
<div data-confirm-action="{{ key }}"
     hx-headers='{"X-CSRF-Token": "{{ request.state.csrf_token }}"}'
     hx-target="this"
     hx-swap="innerHTML">
    <div class="edit-section-content">
        <c-layout-flow gap="md">
            {% if blocked_reason %}
            <c-alert/>
            {% else %}
            <c-paragraph>{{ message }}</c-paragraph>
            {% endif %}
            <div id="confirm-action-error" class="edit-section-error is-hidden"></div>
        </c-layout-flow>
    </div>
    <div class="edit-section-actions">
        {% set lotc_onclick_1 %}closeEditModal(){% endset %}<c-button type="secondary" label="Annuleren"/>
        {# Nothing to confirm when the action is refused up front; the dialog then only
           explains why (the server refuses it too). #}
        {% if not blocked_reason %}
        <c-button type="secondary" label="{{ action.label }}" show-icon="before" icon="{{ action.icon | nldd_icon }}" class="confirm-action-submit"/>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
